  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "A link of appinfo/info.xml leads nowhere:",
        "  <bugs> https://gitlab.com/brewcode-de/brewmemo/nextcloud/-/issues: HTTP 404",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "node-eol",
      "lines": [
        "engines.node ^16.0.0 in package.json admits only end-of-life Node lines: the release is built on Node 16, which reached end of life on 2023-09-11.",
        "  That Node receives no security fixes, and the lockfile is resolved for it. The oldest line still maintained is Node 22.",
        "  Node release dates from schedule.json in nodejs/Release, as of 2026-11-02."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL (composer.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 31 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is brewmemo, the checkout directory is nextcloud.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 31 to 33; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 31 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support-max",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml caps PHP at max-version 8.5.",
        "  A server on a newer PHP refuses to enable the app, so this cap has to be raised deliberately with every PHP release, not left where it was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^16.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.js, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.js), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpintegration.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), EditorConfig (.editorconfig).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.js: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "17 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @editorjs/checklist, @editorjs/delimiter, @editorjs/editorjs, @editorjs/header, @editorjs/image, @editorjs/link, @editorjs/list, @editorjs/marker, and 9 more.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 90 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
      "lines": [
        "Version 0.6.0 in appinfo/info.xml and package.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP 8.2 is the floor in appinfo/info.xml and in composer.json, platform 8.2."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 2) in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    }
